            "description": "<p>Investors can easily look back on the themes that dominated markets (<a data-i13n=\"cpos:1;pos:1\" href=\"https://finance.yahoo.com/quote/%5EDJI?p=%5EDJI&.tsrc=fin-srch\">^DJI</a>, <a data-i13n=\"cpos:2;pos:1\" href=\"https://finance.yahoo.com/quote/%5EIXIC?p=%5EIXIC&.tsrc=fin-srch\">^IXIC</a>, <a data-i13n=\"cpos:3;pos:1\" href=\"https://finance.yahoo.com/quote/%5EGSPC?p=%5EGSPC&.tsrc=fin-srch\">^GSPC</a>) throughout 2025, so what are some of the top investment ideas they should be expecting or watching in 2026? Hint: it's still AI. Or more so, the companies that will be physically building out and powering the AI infrastructure.</p>\n<p>Hennion & Walsh CIO Kevin Mahn tells <a data-i13n=\"cpos:4;pos:1\" href=\"https://www.yahoo.com/author/julie-hyman/?.tsrc=fin-srch\">Julie Hyman</a> how he is \"following the money\" and watching the companies that will ultimately become the true architects of the artificial intelligence buildout.</p>\n<p>To watch more expert insights and analysis on the latest market action, check out more\u00a0<a data-i13n=\"cpos:5;pos:1\" href=\"https://finance.yahoo.com/videos/series/morning-brief/\">Morning Brief</a>.</p>",
